  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe optimized function h(x) must minimize the maximum overlap with its shifted version (1 - h(x)). Current approaches focus on local gradient-based methods (SLSQP), which may converge to local minima. We propose using a combination of differential evolution (DE) and gradient optimization to exploit DE's global search capabilities while using gradient descent for local refinement.\n\nDifferential evolution is chosen for its ability to handle non-convex objectives without derivative information. The strategy combines DE's exploration with local optimization for exploitation. The higher resolution (n_points=100) allows more precise representation of h(x). Initializations include the parent solution, random binary, and structured patterns (sinusoidal, ramp functions).\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: h \u2208 \u211d^{n_points}, 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, sum(h) = n_points / 2\n- Objective: C\u2085 = max_{k} [\u2211 h_i (1 - h_{i-k}) * dx]\n- dx = 2.0 / n_points\n- Correlation computed with np.correlate(h, 1 - h, mode=\"full\") * dx\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialization:\n1. Use initial_h_values as one starting point\n2. Generate random binary patterns\n3. Create sinusoidal patterns with varying frequencies\n4. Construct piecewise linear ramps\n\nb. Differential Evolution:\n1. Set DE parameters (population size, scaling factor, crossover rate)\n2. Clip and rescale population to meet constraints\n3. Evaluate objective and keep track of best solution\n\nc. Gradient descent refinement:\n1. Apply SLSQP to top candidates from DE\n2. Perturb best solution and refine further\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Population size: 20-40\n- DE parameters: scaling=0.8, crossover=0.9\n- Gradient steps: 100-150\n- Initial patterns: 10 diverse forms\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- DE dominates time with ~600s for population evolution\n- Gradient descent: ~300s\n- Budget split: 90% exploration, 10% refinement\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nRequire sum(h) \u2248 n_points/2 and C\u2085 \u2264 0.38085. Final solution must meet evaluation criteria.",
